  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Markets for Change (M4C) Program - Samoa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Markets for Change (M4C) is a UNWomen led multi-country initiative. It supports marketplaces in rural and urban areas to be safe, inclusive and non-discriminatory. The M4C project Phase II aims to make Samoan marketplaces cleaner, greener and safer, with the principal focus of enhancing the economic empowerment of women market vendors. M4C has four end of program outcomes: 1) Inclusive, effective and representative marketplace groups are created to grow, further enabled and recognized; 2) Improved socioeconomic security of women market vendors; 3) Loval governments, market management and other decision-makers are gender-responsive, effective and accountable to women market vendors; and 4) Physical infrastructure and operating systems are improved to make markets more gender-responsive, safer, more accessible, and resilient to disaster risks and climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
